{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass after the death of Abraham, and He blessed, etc.</b> He comforted him with the consolations of mourners. Another interpretation: even though the Holy One, blessed be He, had entrusted the blessings to Abraham, he was afraid to bless Isaac, because he foresaw Esau coming forth from him. He said: Let the Master of the blessings come and bless whomever is good in His eyes. And the Holy One, blessed be He, came and blessed him (Sotah 14)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:24.106165184Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}